      "problem": "Simplify $3\\sqrt[3]{y}-4\\sqrt{y}-7\\sqrt[3]{y}+2\\sqrt{y}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ terms together, and the two $\\sqrt{y}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt[3]{y}-4\\sqrt{y}-7\\sqrt[3]{y}+2\\sqrt{y} & = \\\\ (-4+2)\\sqrt{y}+(3-7)\\sqrt[3]{y} & = \\\\ -2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ and $\\sqrt{y}$ terms.",
